  "review": [
    "The recipe, selection, authored controls, reference sources and product contracts are unchanged from qualified commit 6977247e61. The existing slice validator checks check identities, snapshots and runtime environment for every retained slice.",
    "Convex transport capture and app-origin binding are replaced with 26 fresh controls across 14 affected checks. The clean reference passes 23/23 points and the empty app earns none. Old evidence for those Convex and null checks is excluded.",
    "The removed generic purchase/checkout pending-status assertion imposed an unrequested initial state. Explicit payment/lifecycle checks still enforce their own states. All 624 earlier controls were reclassified from hash-verified grades; no accepted control depended on either removed assertion. Correct references use pending and still pass.",
    "Accepting beforeunload permits the requested reload; normal confirmation dialogs remain dismissed. Prior retained final controls are conclusive app failures. The one historical inconclusive SpacetimeDB reload retry remains recorded and supplies no passing measurement.",
    "Parent-owned resource lease delegation changes launch authorization, not app behavior or scoring; focused reservation and reference contract tests pass. Stop-before-readiness ordering does not change reference sources. Saved backend URI restoration affects regrading only. Pending-request diagnostics and dashboard changes do not change measured outcomes.",
    "174 focused tests passed on Windows and in the frozen Linux image; 30 additional auth-patch, scope, reservation and reference-contract tests passed in Linux. Unaffected controls were not rerun.",
    "Docker MemTotal changed from 49232842752 to 49232826368 bytes (16 KiB) with all other identity fields unchanged. runnerEnvironmentIdentity compares memory at nearest MiB; original byte readings are preserved. Tests reject a 1 MiB capacity change and CPU/kernel changes. This metadata-only change does not alter reference, mutation, or null execution."
